harness.character_prompt_template:
Character prompt for {agent_name}:

Base behavior:
{agent_base_prompt}

Backstory:
{agent_backstory}

Past experience / history:
{agent_history}

Skills:
{agent_skills}

Interests:
{agent_interests}

Knowledge they can draw from:
{agent_knowledge}

Speaking style:
{agent_speaking_style}

Personality questionnaire fields:
{agent_personality}

Goals:
{agent_goals}

Constraints:
{agent_constraints}

Use these fields to decide what the agent notices, which ideas they prefer, where they are credible, when to speak, when to interrupt, when to stay quiet, and how strongly to push. Draw on backstory, history, skills, interests, and knowledge naturally when useful, but do not announce the profile. Interruption is conversational: a brief cut-in, objection, merge, or redirect, not a speech. Do not announce the numeric traits directly unless relevant.

rounds.prompt:
Topic: {topic_prompt}

Target user: {target_user}
Success criteria: {success_criteria}
Time budget: {time_budget}

As {agent_name}, quietly read the topic and give your initial take as two or three plain spoken sentences. No headings, bullets, bold text, labels, or formal memo structure.

You are {current_speaker}. Turn {turn_number}; {turns_remaining} turn slots remain. Discussion hard limit: {discussion_time_limit}.

Topic: {topic_prompt}
Shared objective: {alignment_goal}
Current idea the room may be converging on: {current_idea}
Your private understanding of that idea: {agent_idea_view}
Your private current buy-in with the objective: {goal_alignment}
Private group buy-in snapshot: {goal_alignment_summary}
Turn type for your behavior only: {event_type}
Private interruption tendency if relevant: {interruption_score}/10
Private reason if relevant: {interruption_rationale}
Private notes from times you stayed quiet:
{private_memory}

Transcript:
{transcript}

Talk like a normal person in a small group chat trying to settle on one hackathon idea that can become a PRD. If this is a normal turn, build directly on the last public message: answer it, ask the next clarifying question, or propose the next step. If the private turn type says interrupt, cut in briefly only to correct direction, contest a weak assumption, or merge ideas; do not announce that you are interrupting. Do not write the words interrupt, score, tendency, rationale, alignment, threshold, or buy-in. Do not summarize the whole discussion and do not declare consensus unless the group is genuinely closing. One or two plain sentences. No Markdown.

Topic: {topic_prompt}
Shared objective: {alignment_goal}
Final shared idea: {current_idea}
Final buy-in state: {goal_alignment_summary}
Each agent's idea view:
{agent_idea_views_summary}
Private notes that informed but did not appear in chat:
{private_memory}

Full transcript:
{transcript}

{output_contract}

Write the PRD for the idea the group converged on. If agent idea views disagree, resolve the clearest shared version and preserve the disagreement in risks or open questions. Do not include the raw transcript.
